        overview_kicker: "Start here",
        overview_title: "Reading paths for first-time and advanced users",
        overview_lead: "This section starts with two things: which model/surface choices are current, and where first-time and professional users should begin. Today's edits are kept only in the Changelog near the bottom.",
        overview_update_1_title: "GPT-6 Astra model guidance",
        overview_update_1_desc: "Current recommended models include Astra, Sol, Terra, and Luna. Compare results on the same work and completion criteria, and check your picker and the official Models page for access.",
        overview_update_2_title: "Reasoning effort and scope",
        overview_update_2_desc: "Adjust effort based on results. Dominik’s Astra experiments suggest starting with Light/Low or Medium and defining the deliverable, checks, and handoff.",
        overview_update_3_title: "Fixing Astra picker visibility",
        overview_update_3_desc: "CLI 0.153.4 fixes Astra picker visibility. If it remains missing after updating, check sign-in method, workspace access, and explicitly saved model settings.",
        overview_update_4_title: "Enterprise announcements separated",
        overview_update_4_desc: "The June 11 Codex app 26.609 release adds Plus/Pro rate-limit reset banking, Developer mode for Browser/CDP access, `/init` in the app composer, expanded Enterprise Computer Use, and per-app access controls for Computer Use on Windows. The June 18 Enterprise spend-controls announcement adds Global Admin Console credit usage analytics for ChatGPT and Codex, user/product/model breakdowns, unified Cost API access, and workspace/group/user spend limits, so the guide treats it as Enterprise admin operations. The June 24 AWS announcement is reflected only as an enterprise/provider deployment path for OpenAI models and Codex on Amazon Bedrock. Workspace Agents is separated as a ChatGPT Business/Enterprise/Edu/Teachers research-preview flow for shared cloud agents. The June 28 HP Frontier partnership is recorded only as enterprise adoption context.",
        overview_update_5_title: "Broader launch-post sweep",
        overview_update_5_desc: "I re-read `developers.openai.com/codex`, the Codex changelog, `developers.openai.com/blog`, `openai.com/index`, and `openai.com/codex` together. The August 13 Ultrafast mode preview is separated as a limited preview API `service_tier` for eligible GPT-5.6 Sol workloads. It can return `service_tier=ultrafast`, but it is not a Codex model-picker default or a ChatGPT credit-plan change. The August 5 Fast long-context changelog stays in the GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna API request lane. The August 12 RingCentral story and enterprise research post remain enterprise adoption context. Daybreak Blue/Red, Linux desktop app preview, Business Premium, and the August 6 ChatGPT GPT-5.6 Sol announcement keep their existing boundaries.",
        overview_update_6_title: "Docs MCP, API changelog, and config rechecked",
        overview_update_6_desc: "Docs MCP, the config reference, and app/settings were rechecked around trusted project-scoped `.codex/config.toml`, the user-level requirement for machine-local provider/auth/profile/telemetry routing keys, shared CLI/IDE setup, the AGENTS.md steering snippet, `review_model`, `plan_mode_reasoning_effort`, granular approvals, `approvals_reviewer`, `default_permissions`, permissions profiles, app-level approval modes, sandboxed network proxy/requirements, keyring credential storage, forced login/workspace, `sqlite_home`, and hooks/plugin/skill controls. API hard spend limits now belong in the Platform/API lane because organization or project monthly caps can return 429 once tracked spend reaches the limit. OpenAI API changelog Fast mode long-context support is recorded only as GPT-5.6 Sol/Terra/Luna API requests over 272K tokens still being eligible for Fast mode. Sites remains split clearly: `.openai/hosting.json` stores project linkage and D1/R2 binding names, while runtime secrets are managed in the Sites panel.",
        overview_lens_beginner_kicker: "Beginner at a glance",
        overview_lens_beginner_title: "Smallest path to a real first win",
        overview_lens_beginner_desc: "Lock what “started” means before reading everything.",
