        changelog_kicker: "Changelog",
        changelog_title: "Recent updates",
        changelog_item_1: "Corrected the outdated GPT-5.6 default in model summaries and aligned Astra Power options and client support with the official Models page.",
        changelog_item_2: "Added Dominik’s Astra X article: provide the right apps and references, compare Light/Medium, and define deliverables and checks.",
        changelog_item_3: "The September 4 CLI 0.153.4 release fixes Astra picker visibility and the bundled default when no model is explicitly configured.",
        changelog_item_4: "Re-audited all 101 official use cases. Reflected extra blank-line structure changes across 74 official Starter prompts in both promptEn and promptKo. Local missing cards 0, missing official URLs 0, local `official.promptEn` mismatch 0, promptEn gaps 0, promptKo gaps 0, and line/token structure mismatches 0.",
        changelog_item_5: "Rechecked OpenAI Developers MCP and openai.com/index. The August 13 Ultrafast mode preview is tracked as an eligible GPT-5.6 Sol API service-tier preview, and the August 5 Fast long-context note stays in the Platform/API lane.",
        changelog_item_6: "The guide now follows the new learn.chatgpt.com information architecture. Section 10 no longer mixes incompatible permission configurations, and section 16 now centers Local/Worktree scheduled tasks plus a validated commit/push prompt.",
        overview_update_7_title: "Local automation refresh",
        overview_update_8_title: "Apple Messages approval boundary added",
        changelog_item_7: "Added the Apple Messages plugin's execution and send-approval boundary. It works only in Codex or ChatGPT Work in the ChatGPT desktop app for macOS; review the message and recipients before approving a send.",
        overview_update_9_title: "Added the GitLab cloud beta path",
        changelog_item_8: "Added Codex cloud's GitLab beta. You can connect a GitLab project and environment for `@codex` from issues or merge requests and one-off or automatic reviews, but check webhook permission plus Self-Managed/Dedicated and oversized-diff limits first.",
        overview_update_10_title: "Added read-only thread snapshot sharing",
        changelog_item_9: "Added the macOS desktop flow for choosing the audience in Share or `/share`, selecting Copy link, and reopening the local thread snapshot before sharing it.",
        overview_update_11_title: "Added event-triggered Scheduled task boundary",
        changelog_item_10: "Scheduled tasks triggered by Gmail, Slack, or GitHub events are available only in ChatGPT web and mobile for eligible plans. They do not run against a local desktop project, require app connection and permission, and cannot combine with a time-based schedule.",
        overview_update_12_title: "Added browser extension and Site tools boundaries",
        changelog_item_11: "Added current browser-control support for Edge, Brave, Opera, and Vivaldi alongside Chrome, plus the Sol/Terra-only availability of Site tools (WebMCP) in the In-app browser.",
        overview_update_13_title: "Expanded the iOS remote-work flow",
        changelog_item_12: "Added iOS 1.2026.237 boundaries for attachments across connected hosts, the Priority view, and editable queued-prompt sync.",
        changelog_sources_toggle: "How sources are placed",
        changelog_sources_note: "Instead of keeping one long source dump at the bottom, the guide now points you to the small `Sources` line under each section. The changelog should stay short, while the relevant section holds the links you are most likely to verify next.",
        s1_title: "Codex at a Glance",
        s1_intro: "OpenAI Codex is a coding agent that can read code, make changes, run checks, and explain the result.",
        s1_philosophy: '"From writing code → finishing work"',
        s1_desc: "Model, pricing, and setup details come later. This section only gives you the main surfaces and milestones.",
