        s2_title: "Codex Product Suite at a Glance",
        s2_cli: "Terminal-based (TUI) local agentic coding and CI/CD automation for macOS, Linux, and Windows. On Linux, choose between CLI and the desktop app preview based on the workflow.",
        s2_app: "Codex inside the ChatGPT desktop app for macOS, Windows, and Linux preview. It acts as a command center for agents with built-in worktrees, an integrated terminal, diff review, inline editing/annotations, sidebar PR review, skills, automations, and personality controls. The Linux preview supports Ubuntu 24.04/26.04, Debian 13, Fedora 43/44, and fully updated Arch Linux on x64/ARM64; Computer Use is not yet included there.",
        s2_ide: "IDE agent across VS Code, Cursor, Windsurf, VS Code Insiders, Xcode, and JetBrains with both local work and cloud delegation.",
        s2_cloud: "ChatGPT web/mobile surfaces. Web covers GitHub environments, cloud coding tasks, diff review, automatic PR/code review, and `@codex` delegation. GitLab is in beta for `@codex` from issues or merge requests and one-off or automatic merge-request reviews; the mobile preview lets you continue threads, approvals, model changes, and screenshot/terminal/diff/test review from a phone while Codex runs on a Mac or remote environment.",
