        code_s16_local_prompt: '<code>This is a recurring official-doc refresh for the current local Git repository.\n\nGoal\n- Use learn.chatgpt.com/docs as the primary source for product guidance.\n- Remove outdated explanations and links, and keep the Korean and English content semantically aligned.\n- Leave short examples and verification steps that a real user can follow.\n\nPreflight\n- Check the current branch, git status --short, and remote.\n- If user-owned tracked changes are present or main has diverged from origin/main, do not edit, commit, or push; report why.\n- Do not modify, add, or delete existing untracked files.\n- If git pull --ff-only fails, stop without forcing a resolution.\n\nWork and verification\n- Apply only facts that changed in official docs. Do not add guesses or promotional claims.\n- Edit only relevant files, then run JavaScript syntax checks, translation validation, and git diff --check.\n- Open the local page and inspect Korean, English, and mobile layouts.\n\nPublish\n- Only when every check passes and the diff is limited to this task, stage the relevant tracked files explicitly.\n- Run git commit -m "docs: refresh guide from official ChatGPT docs" and then git push origin main.\n- Do not use git add ., force push, amend, rebase, or delete user files.\n- If push or remote verification is blocked, do not claim success. Report the last successful step and the exact next action needed.</code>',
